Hook When it runs <code>task(me, ctx)</code> Builds a persistent task tree advanced by the fixed-step kernel <code>mission(me, ctx)</code> Declares objectives and completion conditions <code>on_start(me, ctx)</code> Once, after the owner and its required inputs are ready <code>on_event(me, evt, ctx)</code> When an event reaches the owner <code>on_stop(me, ctx)</code> On hot reload, detach, despawn, or scene teardown <code>on_tick(me, ctx)</code> Test-only sampling callback; avoid it in production <p><code>me</code> is the owning entity id. <code>ctx</code> carries scenario parameters and execution context. <code>this</code> is the persistent per-instance state map.</p> <pre><code>fn on_start(me, ctx) {
    this.started = true;
    notify("Mission ready");
}

fn on_event(me, evt, ctx) {
    if evt.name == "MISSION_COMPLETE" {
        notify_kind("Mission complete", "success");
    }
}

fn on_stop(me, ctx) {
    brake(me);
}
</code></pre>
